    # Section 10: Conclusions
    doc.append('<details class="med-details"><summary>')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('## 10. Conclusions</summary><div class="details-content">')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('The use of real-time point-of-care ultrasound for vascular cannulation represents a fundamental patient safety advancement. Integrating ultrasound before, during, and after vessel puncture significantly improves overall and first-pass success, reduces procedural time, and drastically curtails serious mechanical complications across diverse venous and arterial access sites in both adult and pediatric populations.')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('Clinicians must adhere to rigorous procedural standards: performing comprehensive pre-access scans, employing real-time needle visualization with dynamic tip control, and mandating definitive sonographic confirmation of the guidewire within the vascular lumen in two orthogonal planes prior to dilation. Institutional investment in simulation-based education and standardized credentialing is essential to translate these recommendations into uniform clinical excellence.')
